      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_11",
        on: "start",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("The party traveled down the river for days, sometimes walking through the shallow water, sometimes swimming, helped by the merfolk."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("One day they saw a gruesome sight — a fleet of boats and rafts sunk or shattered among the river islands. Konrad sent some of the merfolk to investigate."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "merman-advisor",
            text: _("These are not proper ships, but shallow-draft boats built only recently; much of their timber is green. They were sunk in battle, not by a storm. Those that were not capsized have been burned. The battle must have taken place not long ago, perhaps only a few weeks past. We’ve found no survivors. One more thing...all flew the banner of the Crown of Wesnoth."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Delfador",
            text: _("Haven’t you found any enemy boats, ones the Wesnothians were fighting against?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "merman-advisor",
            text: _("No, we have not. If there were any, they are long gone."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Li'sar",
            text: _("Perhaps the monsters Lord Kalenz alluded to sunk the boats."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Kalenz",
            text: _("That is possible. I would guess they were seeking a way east, just as we are."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            text: _("What do we do next? How much more of the river do we still have to travel?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Delfador",
            text: _("The mountains north and south of the river are impassable."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Li'sar",
            text: _("Then we have only two choices: to proceed down the river or to go back where we came from and fight our way through the orcs or the undead."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Delfador",
            text: _("We certainly have no time to go back! We must hurry to the home of the North Elves, to meet with our elven allies."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            text: _("Delfador is right. We must go on!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:delay",
            time: 1000,
          },
          {
            tag: "spawn",
            id: "Keh_Ohn",
            type: "Armageddon Drake",
            side: 2,
            x: 3,
            y: 8,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:spawn_unit",
            unit: "Keh_Ohn",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            text: _("Oh my! A monster!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Li'sar",
            text: _("A dragon! A big one!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Keh Ohn",
            text: _("I am Keh Ohn, leader of the drakes who have settled upon these cliffs. Who are you?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            text: _("A talking dragon?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Li'sar",
            text: _("I am beginning to understand why you were talking about monsters on our way here, Lord Kalenz."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "merman-advisor",
            text: _("With all due respect, Your Highnesses, you are both wrong. This is not a dragon. This is a drake."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Delfador",
            text: _("Here? But, drakes have never been seen in Wesnoth before... Are you certain of this?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "merman-advisor",
            text: _("I was born in the Bay of Pearls and spent my entire life on the Eastern Shore. But I have spoken with those who have traveled the Western Ocean and met drakes on their journeys. Therefore, I am certain beyond doubt that the creature flying in front of us is a drake, Delfador. Concerning the drakes having never been seen in Wesnoth, must I remind you that we are not in Wesnoth anymore? There are many unthinkable things and creatures which can be found outside of Wesnoth."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Keh Ohn",
            text: _("GRROAR!! Will you silly self-centered creatures show some manners and pay some attention to me?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            text: _("Eh... well of course, Sir Drake. Let me introduce myself — I am Prince Konrad, leader of the group and heir to the throne of Wesnoth."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Li'sar",
            text: _("And I am the Princess, Li’sar, the only daughter of the late King Garard II and Queen Asheviere. I, too, am an heir to the throne of Wesnoth!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Keh Ohn",
            text: _("(releasing a torrent of fire towards Konrad and Li’sar) Soooo... It is you who sent your subordinates to attack us. Now when we’ve destroyed them, you come to do the job yourselves."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            text: _("No...There is an ongoing civil war amongst us humans. The boats were sent by our enemies, not by us, even if they were Wesnothian boats."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Kalenz",
            text: _("The Prince speaks the truth."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Keh Ohn",
            text: _("I don’t know. Maybe you are telling the truth, maybe not. We drakes don’t trust you. Many of our warriors died in the battle and many more are still healing their wounds, but we still have claws. Go back now and leave us in peace. If you go further we’ll be forced to show them."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Delfador",
            text: _("But we cannot go back. We are on an important mission."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Keh Ohn",
            text: _("If you defy my warning — prepare for battle."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Konrad",
            text: _("So be it. We have to go down the river; we have no choice. We’ll fight our way through if necessary."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Keh Ohn",
            text: _("You will regret challenging us. Drakes, to arms!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:delay",
            time: 500,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:kill_unit",
            filter: "%7B%22tag%22%3A%22kill%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%7B%22x%22%3A%224%22%2C%22y%22%3A%229%22%2C%22animate%22%3A%22no%22%7D%2C%22children%22%3A%5B%5D%7D",
          },
          {
            tag: "spawn",
            id: "Keh_Ohn",
            type: "Armageddon Drake",
            side: 2,
            x: 27,
            y: 8,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:spawn_unit",
            unit: "Keh_Ohn",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
